                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1470-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ></span>DPA 4041-S</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Pencil Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The DPA 4041-S is a modular omnidirectional microphone consisting of two parts:</p><ul><li>B&amp;K MMC4041 capsule head: 24mm, stainless-steel diaphragm, capable of 10-20kHz response with only 7dBA self-noise</li><li>MMP4000-S solid-state head amplifier, with 7-pin XLRM connector</li></ul><p>The combination requires DPA&#8217;s high-voltage power supply, p/n HMA5000, which can power 2 microphones at 130V apiece as well as providing +30dB of amplifier gain, specified at +0dB/-1dB from 10Hz&ndash;100kHz.</p><p>Although the capsule head is detachable from the head amp, neither B&amp;K nor DPA manufactures other capsules that fit this head amp. The MMC4041 head can be used on DPA&#8217;s other 4041-series head amps, as well as B&amp;K measurement equipment.</p><p>Surprisingly, although this mic runs at 130V, the B&amp;K capsule is a pre-polarized electret model.</p><p>Note that there are two other 4041 head amplifiers from this mic series:</p><ul><li><b>MMP4000-SP</b> (MSRP $3198) - phantom-powered head amp</li><li><b>MMP4000-T</b> (MSRP $3331) - head amp with tube circuit</li></ul><p><p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/DPA/4041-S">DPA 4041-S</a></p>
